WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.139
One day Robin was talking to Will Scarlet.

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.707
"We're running low on money. How will we help the poor?"

3
00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:13.636
"What about a feast?" asked Will.

4
00:00:13.637 --> 00:00:20.874
"Yes!" said Robin. "Go find a rich man and bring him to eat with us."

5
00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:24.380
Will and several men went to the road and waited.

6
00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:28.354
Many people passed by, but there were no rich people.

7
00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:36.536
The men ate some lunch and took a nap, and at last the sun began to set.

8
00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:39.093
"Let's go home," said Will.

9
00:00:39.094 --> 00:00:43.023
The men had just started walking when Will stopped abruptly.

10
00:00:43.024 --> 00:00:45.743
"Shh. I hear something!"

11
00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.933
The others listened and soon they heard it too.

12
00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:53.735
A young man sat by a stream, crying!

13
00:00:53.736 --> 00:00:58.143
His blond hair was messy and his clothes looked rumpled.

14
00:00:58.144 --> 00:01:02.701
Over his head a wooden harp hung from a tree branch.

15
00:01:02.702 --> 00:01:05.850
"You're Alan of Dale, the minstrel," said Will.

16
00:01:05.851 --> 00:01:11.338
"Yes." Alan reached for his harp with a sigh.

17
00:01:11.339 --> 00:01:14.578
"What's wrong?" asked Will.

18
00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:18.462
"I want to marry a beautiful girl named Ellen.

19
00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:21.509
Her father doesn't like me because I'm poor.

20
00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:28.922
This morning I learned some terrible news—she's marrying Sir Stephen of Trent.

21
00:01:28.923 --> 00:01:32.466
He's an old man, but he's rich.

22
00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.460
And the wedding's in two days!"

23
00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.834
"Come home with us," said Will.

24
00:01:37.835 --> 00:01:41.737
"I'm sure Robin Hood can find a way to help you."

25
00:01:41.738 --> 00:01:46.315
They walked through the forest and soon arrived at the big oak tree.

26
00:01:46.316 --> 00:01:49.893
"You didn't bring me a rich man," said Robin.

27
00:01:49.894 --> 00:01:55.147
"No," said Will. "This is Alan of Dale, and he has a problem."

28
00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:58.732
Robin listened carefully to Alan's story.

29
00:01:58.733 --> 00:02:02.461
The young man was obviously full of sorrow.

30
00:02:02.462 --> 00:02:05.154
"I think I have a plan," said Robin.

31
00:02:05.155 --> 00:02:10.400
"But tell me something first—are you sure Ellen wants to marry you?"

32
00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:14.750
"Oh, yes!" Alan replied. "We're engaged."

33
00:02:14.751 --> 00:02:17.537
"Then the solution is simple," said Robin.

34
00:02:17.538 --> 00:02:20.442
"All we need is a friar to marry you."

35
00:02:20.443 --> 00:02:23.380
"I know the friar of Fountain Abbey," said Will.

36
00:02:23.381 --> 00:02:25.355
"Robin, I'll guide you to the abbey."

37
00:02:25.356 --> 00:02:27.954
"I'll go tomorrow morning," Robin said.

38
00:02:27.955 --> 00:02:30.076
"And don't worry, Alan.

39
00:02:30.077 --> 00:02:35.532
You'll soon be married to the lovely Ellen!"

40
00:02:35.533 --> 00:02:38.685
The next day Will led Robin to a river.

41
00:02:38.686 --> 00:02:40.187
"I'll leave you here.

42
00:02:40.188 --> 00:02:41.949
The abbey is easy to find.

43
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.772
You can cross the river just around the bend."

44
00:02:44.773 --> 00:02:50.293
Robin walked along the river and soon spotted a stout man—a friar.

45
00:02:50.294 --> 00:02:53.017
He had curly black hair and red cheeks.

46
00:02:53.018 --> 00:02:56.374
His gray eyes danced with humor.

47
00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.832
"Hello!" called Robin.

48
00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:01.254
"Do you know the friar of Fountain Abbey?"

49
00:03:01.255 --> 00:03:05.193
"Yes, somewhat," answered the friar.

50
00:03:05.194 --> 00:03:09.236
"I believe I must cross the river to find him," Robin went on.

51
00:03:09.237 --> 00:03:12.575
"But I don't want to get my nice clothes wet.

52
00:03:12.576 --> 00:03:16.703
You look very strong. Will you carry me across?"

53
00:03:16.704 --> 00:03:19.267
"What?" cried the friar.

54
00:03:19.268 --> 00:03:24.238
Then he remembered he was a religious man and should do good deeds.

55
00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:26.928
"Fine. I'll do it," he said.

56
00:03:26.929 --> 00:03:31.320
"Let me carry your sword so it stays dry."

57
00:03:31.321 --> 00:03:35.844
Robin gave the friar his sword and climbed onto the man's back.

58
00:03:35.845 --> 00:03:39.123
They crossed the river.

59
00:03:39.124 --> 00:03:43.453
On the other side, the friar looked slyly at Robin.

60
00:03:43.454 --> 00:03:46.481
"I want to return to the other side.

61
00:03:46.482 --> 00:03:49.064
But I'm too wet and tired.

62
00:03:49.065 --> 00:03:54.250
Now it's your turn—you must carry me back across."

63
00:03:54.251 --> 00:03:58.172
"What?" This time Robin was outraged.

64
00:03:58.173 --> 00:04:01.846
But the friar refused to return Robin's sword.

65
00:04:01.847 --> 00:04:08.241
So Robin had no choice but to pick up the friar and carry him across the river.

66
00:04:08.242 --> 00:04:11.571
"Where's my sword?" asked the friar.

67
00:04:11.572 --> 00:04:18.035
"Right here!" Robin had managed to seize the friar's sword as well as his own sword.

68
00:04:18.036 --> 00:04:22.796
"I'll give it to you. But you must carry me across the river again."

69
00:04:22.797 --> 00:04:26.132
"Fine," grumbled the friar.

70
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:28.527
He picked up Robin.

71
00:04:28.528 --> 00:04:32.515
Halfway across the river, the friar stopped for a moment.

72
00:04:32.516 --> 00:04:39.744
Then, with a sudden lift of his hand, he dumped Robin into the water.

73
00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:48.281
Robin leaped up and the men began to fight on land with swords.

74
00:04:48.282 --> 00:04:51.125
The two men fought for a long time.

75
00:04:51.126 --> 00:04:55.238
At last Robin blew his horn three times.

76
00:04:55.239 --> 00:04:58.677
Will Scarlet appeared with a large group of men.

77
00:04:58.678 --> 00:05:05.244
But the friar whistled loudly and suddenly four fierce dogs ran at Robin!

78
00:05:05.245 --> 00:05:09.582
They chased him up a tree.

79
00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:13.154
"Help!" cried Robin.

80
00:05:13.155 --> 00:05:16.453
Will stepped forward to call the dogs.

81
00:05:16.454 --> 00:05:20.527
They instantly ran to him and licked his face.

82
00:05:20.528 --> 00:05:23.925
"Will?" cried the friar in surprise.

83
00:05:23.926 --> 00:05:27.922
"Is that you? What are you doing here?"

84
00:05:27.923 --> 00:05:33.887
"I brought Robin Hood to meet you," said Will.

85
00:05:33.888 --> 00:05:36.099
Robin climbed down the tree.

86
00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:41.402
"Robin," said Will. "This is Friar Tuck, the friar of Fountain Abbey!"

87
00:05:41.403 --> 00:05:44.708
The two men laughed and shook hands.

88
00:05:44.709 --> 00:05:50.333
"I need your help, Friar," Robin said. "Please come home with us."

